13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416433 1077 "selection" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416433 1078 #edb/ref 17592186416429 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416433 1079 #uuid "e35daaf4-8a57-5507-af06-07e8ca410d81" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416408 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416413 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416416 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416419 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416425 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1077 "selection" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1078 #edb/ref 17592186416408 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416434 1079 #uuid "fd23a28f-9c20-551f-9dfa-96e071ee475a" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416435 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416434 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416435 1069 "q-131586" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416435 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416435 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+3z=1 \\\\  & y-2z=-1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416435 1072 #uuid "2ad315bd-aaaa-532d-a173-690fb5924119" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416435 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=-5 \\\\  & y=3 \\\\  & z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=-5$, $y=3$, and $z=2.$" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416436 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416433 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416436 1069 "q-74618" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416436 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416436 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+5z=1 \\\\ -x+4y-3z=-1 \\\\ 6y+12z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416436 1072 #uuid "6ba94d2c-82a9-5b70-84fa-d478e1834095" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416436 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416430 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416437 1069 "q-131636" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416437 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416437 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z=6 \\\\ x+y+z=10 \\\\ -4x-8y-4z=-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416437 1072 #uuid "751f8e53-b86d-5abb-abe8-9ed7db35005a" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416437 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ -4 & -8 & -4 & -24\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ -4 & -8 & -4 & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -8 & -4 & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416438 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416432 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416438 1069 "q-74616" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416438 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416438 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+6y-9z=1 \\\\ 4x+24y-36z=4 \\\\ 2x+12y-18z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416438 1072 #uuid "936fd617-fd7c-5014-a3dd-661b242ff833" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true] [17592186416438 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 24 & -36 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 12 & -18 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 24 & -36 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 12 & -18 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 12 & -18 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+6y-9z=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-6y+9z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-6y+9z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534260 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0f53140c-1654-5c33-b318-d2cc5cdbf3e7" 17592186416405 "answer-304b1dcf-fe68-5a04-9923-993bb9c2600c" 17592186416406 "answer-37f8b70e-8988-548d-a3be-78d70d320ac5" 17592186416407 "answer-3af2aed8-fdfb-58cb-b98c-201c2c75c6e9" 17592186416408 "answer-3b8ed053-8c5f-5809-b29d-46bc30062dd8" 17592186416409 "answer-41de81ea-84fe-5b61-b75f-9ba0d3cf554f" 17592186416410 "answer-52ed3b97-c09d-5bac-bedf-d8cb30fd9295" 17592186416411 "answer-5960393e-9030-557e-ab5d-a3d7e339e745" 17592186416412 "answer-6a3aeef0-3b42-5088-81d5-6224943b8101" 17592186416413 "answer-6db75576-d1ba-5d48-ac44-154afca38038" 17592186416414 "answer-75f1836d-e176-5604-8225-6583350f7fb8" 17592186416415 "answer-96134954-26b0-550f-90ea-4210c359ce29" 17592186416416 "answer-96dbb4c2-3f9e-56bc-bd75-793f5331038b" 17592186416417 "answer-a3856c48-bf2a-5bc5-9868-35836353e134" 17592186416418 "answer-a47dea73-bd87-5856-8071-fe09e1271cdf" 17592186416419 "answer-a79f9ab6-7ac4-5781-9305-8bf872102b01" 17592186416420 "answer-ac17277b-e3d6-5ce0-80fb-9b8b2c10fe27" 17592186416421 "answer-ac656c16-72de-5990-8b14-ea78597ee501" 17592186416422 "answer-ad204329-d0a2-52cb-bab5-d155cba3473f" 17592186416423 "answer-c007e82d-17a9-51fa-8a38-a771c858fc7a" 17592186416424 "answer-ee09aac2-7ab9-5ad7-9ffb-67373e750c08" 17592186416425 "answer-ef5cb930-e60b-5fab-bb06-77c743c66a87" 17592186416426 "answer-f9920f96-3b16-549b-9089-4a0bac0aa12e" 17592186416427 "answer-fa5e31d8-6742-527d-a027-3e41d829bbd4" 17592186416428 "answer-fb1ba51a-5f8c-5ab3-961b-4979eb2f83b3" 17592186416429 "answer-field-13c3a85a-1ac4-5ef6-9101-86dc8058f179" 17592186416430 "answ